+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/invest/llc/#article","headline":"Buying and holding a Myrtle Beach rental in a South Carolina LLC","description":"A South Carolina LLC costs $110 to form. Deeding your rental into a single-member LLC owes no recording fee and keeps its tax value. DSCR loans close in the LLC.","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/invest/llc/","author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/about/#devin-day","name":"Devin Day","jobTitle":"Operations Officer","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/about/","worksFor":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"}},"reviewedBy":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/about/#timmy-nash","name":"Timothy Nash","alternateName":"Tim Nash","jobTitle":"Broker-in-Charge","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/about/","worksFor":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"}},"publisher":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"},"datePublished":"2026-09-07","dateModified":"2026-11-09","inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://chapter3realty.com/og-image.jpg","mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/invest/llc/"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Holding a Myrtle Beach rental property in a South Carolina LLC"},"keywords":"buying rental property in an LLC South Carolina, DSCR loan LLC Myrtle Beach, one LLC per rental property, transfer rental to LLC South Carolina deed recording fee, LLC property tax reassessment South Carolina, LLC 4 percent legal residence South Carolina, South Carolina LLC filing fee"}</script>
 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need an LLC for a DSCR loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every DSCR and business-purpose program closes in the name of an LLC or a corporation, according to a loan officer at our preferred lender. The lender requires it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I form a new LLC for each house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most investors here do. About nine in ten Chapter3 investor clients form a new LLC for each house, so a claim at one property stops at that property. Each LLC costs $110 to file and keeps its own books."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can my LLC get a conventional mortgage?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Conventional loans are made to people. A business-purpose loan such as a DSCR loan closes in the LLC name. Deeding a house with a conventional loan to your LLC is a question for the servicer, in writing, before you record."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I move my house into an LLC after closing on a conventional loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"With the servicer's written approval, yes, and that includes a home you live in. Many servicers allow a transfer to an LLC the borrower controls and require the deed back before a refinance. Renting out a house you told the lender you would live in is the problem, and it is mortgage fraud."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I pay the deed recording fee when I move my rental into my LLC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not for a single-member LLC that is ignored for tax. A multi-member LLC taxed as a partnership owes none when the only consideration is an interest in the company. A deed from a partnership or corporation back to an owner pays the fee."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will my property taxes go up if I deed the house to my LLC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not for a deed to a single-member LLC, not taxed as a corporation, by its single member. A deed to a multi-member LLC is exempt only when the contribution is tax-free under the federal partnership rule. Selling more than half of the LLC later triggers a reassessment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to form an LLC in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The filing fee for the articles of organization is $110. An online filing adds a $15 electronic records charge. An LLC that is not taxed as a corporation files no annual report and pays no license fee."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does an LLC lower the income tax on my rental?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. A single-member LLC is disregarded and the rental stays on your Schedule E. A multi-member LLC files a partnership return and the income passes to the members."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the state withhold tax when my LLC sells?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If the members live outside South Carolina, yes. A partnership-taxed LLC is withheld at the top individual rate, 5.21 percent for a 2026 sale. A corporation-taxed LLC is withheld at 5 percent. A disregarded LLC is withheld as its owner."}}]}</script>
