 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays the rent on a Section 8 rental?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The housing authority pays its share by direct deposit each month, and the tenant pays the rest directly to you. The authority's share is the payment standard minus the tenant's share, or the rent minus the tenant's share if the rent is lower."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does Section 8 pay for a 3 bedroom in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The federal fair market rent for three bedrooms is $1,823 for fiscal year 2027. Each housing authority adopts a payment standard between 90 and 110 percent of it. Ask the authority for its current table. The tenant's share comes out of that number."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it hard to find a Section 8 tenant in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The two authorities hold 1,033 vouchers. The Conway waiting list is closed. The Myrtle Beach list last opened in 2022 for two days and drew 1,000 names by lottery. The gate is the inspection and the rent check, not the tenant."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I get the house approved before I find a tenant?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The authority inspects for a specific family and a specific lease after you accept a voucher holder. There is no list of pre-approved houses."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I evict a Section 8 tenant?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, for nonpayment of the tenant's share, for serious or repeated lease violations, and for other good cause, through the court like any eviction. Send the housing authority a copy of the notice."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a tenant lose the voucher for damaging the house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The authority may end assistance for damage beyond ordinary wear, and it must end it if you evict the family through the court for a serious lease violation. It may refuse a new voucher for five years after such an eviction, and while the family owes a housing authority money."}}]}</script>
