/text><line x1="256" y1="212" x2="256" y2="217" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="256" y="234" text-anchor="middle">30</text><line x1="316" y1="212" x2="316" y2="217" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="316" y="234" text-anchor="middle">40</text><text class="ct" x="193" y="250" text-anchor="middle">Days after the storm came ashore</text></svg><figcaption>Daily average height on the river gauge at the Conway Marina. After Florence, the river stayed above flood stage for 29 days, 20 of them in major flood.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">During Florence, the county closed 58 streets in and at the edge of the city for flooding. Long Avenue, Third Avenue, Church Street and Marina Drive stayed closed about four weeks.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which streets flood at each river height</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The National Weather Service lists what floods as the river rises on the gauge:</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">River height</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What floods</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">14 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Low areas along Long Avenue and Sherwood Drive, near Crabtree Swamp</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The Conway Marina, Elm Street and Marina Drive</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">17 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Main Street and Pecan Grove Boulevard may begin to flood</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">21 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The US 501 Bypass may flood. Florence reached about 21 feet.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where Florence's water reached, by subdivision</h3><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Subdivision, and where it is</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Homes Florence's water reached</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Sherwood, around Crabtree Swamp</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">98 of 126</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Midland, just north of downtown</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">33 of 49</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Pecan Grove, west and south</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">29 of 103</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Country Club Forest, around Crabtree Swamp</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">21 of 57</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Lakeland, just north of downtown</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">18 of 37</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">By the county's map, Florence's water did not reach large parts of Conway. No home in Rosehaven, Oak Glenn, Woodland Lakes, Rivertown Row, Kingston Bay or Snowhill is in either flood map.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How often it happens</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Of the 14 floods on record that reached major flood stage at Conway, 6 came in the last 11 years.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For Florence, flood insurance paid 109 claims in the city, and the middle claim was about $134,000. After Hurricane Matthew, the city used FEMA grants to buy 86 buildings. Land bought this way must stay open space.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our page on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how to find out if a house flooded</a> shows every record we use.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">The flood maps for one Conway house</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us a house you like. We check it against FEMA's flood map and the map of where Florence's water reached, before you make an offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check a house for flooding</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="flood-insurance"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood insurance">Do you need flood insurance in Conway, and what does it cost?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Federal law makes a lender require it only when the house is in FEMA's high-risk zone. A lender can still ask for it anywhere.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Outside the high-risk zone, a flood policy on a house usually costs about $560 to $680 a year, depending on the ZIP code.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Flood policy a year, about</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">ZIP 29526</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">ZIP 29527</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Outside the zone</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$560</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$680</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Inside the zone</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$980</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$980</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A new federal flood policy takes effect 30 days after the application and payment are complete, unless it is bought when a home loan is made. Buy it with the house, not when a storm is coming.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does it cost to own a home in Conway each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a typical $265,000 house you live in inside the city, the property tax is about $1,700 a year, plus a flood policy if you want one.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Each year, for a $265,000 house</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">What you pay</th><th scope="col">Inside the city</th><th scope="col">Just outside it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Property tax, a home you live in</th><td data-label="Inside the city">About $1,700</td><td data-label="Just outside it">About $1,100, with an $89 county fee</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Flood policy outside the high-risk zone, if you want one</th><td data-label="Inside the city">About $560 to $680</td><td data-label="Just outside it">About $560 to $680</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tax and flood policy together</th><td data-label="Inside the city">About $2,300 to $2,400</td><td data-label="Just outside it">About $1,600 to $1,700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Property tax instead, as a second home or rental</th><td data-label="Inside the city">About $4,300</td><td data-label="Just outside it">About $3,300</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homeowners insurance is a third bill, on top of these. Its price depends on the house, its roof and the company. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance page</a> explains the policies a house here can need.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina taxes a home you live in on 4 percent of its value, and a second home or rental on 6 percent. You must apply for the lower rate. Inside the city, that makes a rental's bill about 2.5 times a home's. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax page</a> shows how to apply.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">The yearly bills on one house, before you offer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Pick a house. We work out its property tax at the rate you will pay and get you an insurance quote on it.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us price the yearly bills</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="home-prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Home prices">What do homes cost in Conway, SC?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house or townhouse that resold inside the city in the past year usually went for about $265,000. Half sold for between about $220,000 and $340,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At that price, a house in the city is usually three bedrooms and about 1,400 square feet. That is what we found among the houses for sale inside the city near that price at our last count, about 3 in 4 of them with three bedrooms. Some were new, built in the last two years.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Builders sold about 120 new homes in the city in the same year, for about $295,000 in the middle. Few resales were condos, and those went for about $150,000.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a home usually resold for in the past year"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a home usually resold for in the past year</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Town, homes resold</span><span role="columnheader">Middle price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Loris</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">36 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.559" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$235,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Aynor</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">17 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.613" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$255,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">327 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.632" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$265,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Socastee</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">296 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.694" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$290,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">1,004 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.73" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$305,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">All of Horry County</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">8,569 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.777" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$325,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Carolina Forest</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">418 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.95" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$395,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">961 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$420,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Houses and townhouses resold by their owners, not by a builder, and not condo units. Middle price: half sold for more, half for less. Aynor had only 17 resales.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway is not the cheapest town in the county. Homes in Loris and Aynor, two smaller inland towns, resold for less.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At our last count, about 670 houses were for sale with a Conway address, more than half of them new construction, and about 60 on an acre or more. Our <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">no-HOA homes guide</a> and <a href="/buyers/affordable-places-to-live/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">most affordable places</a> include Conway.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="renting-out"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting out">What do homes rent for in Conway?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">HUD's fair market rent for a three-bedroom in the Conway ZIP codes is $1,630 a month. HUD counts rent and utilities together, so the rent alone is less. The figure sits a little under the middle of the market.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Bedrooms</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">HUD fair market rent, ZIPs 29526 and 29527</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,320</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Three</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,630</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Four</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,900</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Carolina Forest's ZIP code, the three-bedroom figure is about $600 more.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In our experience, students near the college look for the cheapest house that fits their group. People moving to be near the college pay more for a nice house close to campus.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In our experience near the college, August is the best month to find a new tenant, because new students arrive. Start marketing a month before the lease ends. Our <a href="/invest/student-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">student rental guide</a> covers renting near Coastal Carolina.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For any address, our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental analyzer</a> gives the rent and the costs. For nightly rentals, see <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what a nightly rental earns by town</a> and <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the short-term rental rules by town</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">What one Conway house would rent for</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us an address. We send back the rent from nearby rentals, the tax at a landlord's rate, and what is left each month after the tax and costs.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us estimate a house's rent</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="pros-and-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in Conway?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The good points are the price, the downtown and the university. The hard ones are flooding in a few places, the city tax and the drive to the beach.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Homes cost less than in the county as a whole, and new homes and land are for sale.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>A downtown on the river, with Main Street, the Riverwalk and Riverfront Park.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>A university and the hospital inside the city, and city trash pickup each week.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>A few parts flood, and the river stays high for weeks.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The city's property tax is higher than just outside it.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The beach is a drive of about 25 minutes, not a walk.</span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="conway-sc-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Conway, SC FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Conway, SC a good place to live?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a buyer who wants a river town with a downtown and a university, at prices under the county's middle, yes. The trade is the drive: the beach is about 25 minutes away by car.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is Conway from Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 25 minutes by car from downtown Conway to the beach in Myrtle Beach, without traffic, and about 27 minutes to Myrtle Beach International Airport.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does Conway, SC flood?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In a few places. About 95 in 100 homes in the city are outside both FEMA's high-risk zone and the land Florence's water reached; most of the rest are near the Waccamaw River, Crabtree Swamp and Kingston Lake.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax rate in Conway, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, a home you live in pays about $654 a year for every $100,000 of the county's value for it. Just outside the city, it pays about $368, plus an $89 county stormwater fee. A second home or rental pays about 2.5 times as much inside the city.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many people live in Conway, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 30,600 in 2025, by the Census Bureau's estimate, up from 24,849 at the 2020 Census.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Conway, SC safe?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. Inside the city limits, the City of Conway has its own police department and fire department.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which schools serve Conway, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County Schools assigns schools by address, and one of its attendance areas is named Conway. We look up the assigned schools for any house you like.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/popest/datasets/2020-2025/cities/totals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census estimates</a>, <a href="https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/CNWS1" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NWS river gauge</a>, <a href="https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/02110704/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USGS gauge</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-claims-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood claims</a>, <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/smallarea/index.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD rents</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 USC 4012a</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4013" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 USC 4013</a>, <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-44/chapter-I/subchapter-D/part-80/section-80.19" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">44 CFR 80.19</a>, <a href="https://www.conwaysc.gov/residents_visitors/about_conway/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City history</a>, <a href="https://www.conwaysc.gov/departments/parks___recreation/parks.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city parks</a>, <a href="https://www.conwaysc.gov/departments/sanitation.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city trash</a>, <a href="https://www.solidwasteauthority.org/recyclingcenters.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county recycling</a>, <a href="https://www.conwaymedicalcenter.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">hospital</a>, <a href="https://www.hgtc.edu/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HGTC</a>, <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/71000785" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NRHP record</a>, <a href="https://nces.ed.gov/collegenavigator/?id=218724" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCES</a>. Our counts from county parcels, flood maps and the past year's deeds. Listing counts in aggregate from CCMLS. Drives from downtown, without traffic.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The boardwalk along the Waccamaw River, at the edge of downtown Conway. Photo: Pubdog, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waccamaw_River_Warehouse_Historic_District_Jun_10.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Conway City Hall on Main Street, once the county courthouse. Photo: Pollinator at en.wikipedia, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferre