gazebo.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wooden boardwalk with a black railing under tall sycamores, beside old wooden buildings on the river in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>The boardwalk along the Waccamaw River, at the edge of downtown Conway.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="c3-cw-side" style="--cw-rows:auto 1fr"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway was laid out in 1732, as Kingston, and later named Conwayborough for General Robert Conway of the state militia.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">City Hall on Main Street was finished in 1825 as the county courthouse. Its design is credited to Robert Mills, who designed the Washington Monument.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-hall-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-hall-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-hall-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="800" alt="Conway City Hall, a brick building with a white portico of four columns and stairs up both sides, beside a white clock tower and palmetto trees" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pollinator at en.wikipedia. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Pollinator at en.wikipedia</a></span></div><figcaption>Conway City Hall on Main Street, once the county courthouse.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Coastal Carolina University is inside the city, about 10 minutes from downtown. It enrolled more than 11,000 students in fall 2024, a record for the school. Horry-Georgetown Technical College has its Conway campus on US 501, and Conway Medical Center is about 10 minutes from downtown.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city is growing fast. By Census estimates it grew about 22 percent since 2020, the seventh fastest among South Carolina cities and towns of 10,000 people or more.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach is about 25 minutes away by car, and the airport about 27.</p><figure class="c3-cw-fig" style="max-width:560px"><div class="c3-cw-frame"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-downtown-conway" viewBox="0 0 360 380" width="360" height="380" role="img" aria-label="Map of Conway and the coast: from downtown Conway, the beach in Myrtle Beach is about 25 minutes by car, the airport about 27 minutes, and Coastal Carolina University and Conway Medical Center about 10 minutes each." style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:760px;background:#f7f3ec;border:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.15)"><style>#c3r-downtown-conway text{font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;paint-order:stroke;stroke:#f7f3ec;stroke-width:3px;stroke-linejoin:round;fill:#1c2028}#c3r-downtown-conway .h{font:500 17px 'Fraunces',Georgia,serif}#c3r-downtown-conway .l{font-size:14px;font-weight:500}#c3r-downtown-conway .m{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;fill:#91592b}#c3r-downtown-conway .t{font-size:14px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.1em;